      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f8b081af-6273-5076-84a9-b794b831a02d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Apple Dumpling Gang, Something Wicked This Way Comes, Winnie the Pooh and the Honey Tree, The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again, The Shaggy D.A., The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh, The Fox and the Hound\n- People: Buddy Baker, Bill Bixby, Jack Clayton, Ray Bradbury, Richard M. Sherman, Robert B. Sherman, Paul J. Smith\n- Organizations: Walt Disney Productions\n- Concepts: California Gold Rush\n\nFacts:\n- Buddy Baker was an American composer who lived from January 4, 1918, to July 26, 2002.\n- In 1975, Walt Disney Productions produced The Apple Dumpling Gang, an American comedy-western film about gambler Russell Donovan, played by Bill Bixby, who is forced to care for orphans that later strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\n- In 1975, Buddy Baker and Paul J. Smith were among the composers who scored Disney films including The Apple Dumpling Gang.\n- In 1975, the songs for Winnie the Pooh and the Honey Tree were written by the Sherman Brothers, Richard M. Sherman and Robert B. Sherman, and its score was composed and conducted by Buddy Baker.\n- In 1979, Buddy Baker scored the Disney film The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again.\n- In 1981, Buddy Baker scored the Disney film The Fox and the Hound.\n- In 1983, Walt Disney Productions produced Something Wicked This Way Comes, an American horror fantasy film directed by Jack Clayton from a screenplay by Ray Bradbury based on Bradbury's novel of the same name.\n- Buddy Baker also scored the Disney films The Shaggy D.A. in 1976 and The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh in 1977.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "42da8ed2-8caf-5985-bd92-e957f878a63c",
        "text": "Page: The Apple Dumpling Gang (film). Sentence: The Apple Dumpling Gang is a 1975 American comedy-western film produced by Walt Disney Productions about a slick gambler named Russell Donovan (Bill Bixby) who is duped into taking care of a group of orphans who eventually strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\nPage: Something Wicked This Way Comes (film). Sentence: Something Wicked This Way Comes is a 1983 American horror fantasy film directed by Jack Clayton and produced by Walt Disney Productions from a screenplay written by Ray Bradbury, based on his novel of the same name.\nPage: Buddy Baker (composer). Sentence: Norman Dale \"Buddy\" Baker (January 4, 1918 – July 26, 2002) was an American composer who, together with Paul J. Smith, scored many Disney films, such as \"The Apple Dumpling Gang\" in 1975, \"The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again\" in 1979, \"The Shaggy D.A.\" in 1976, \"The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh\" in 1977, and \"The Fox and the Hound\" in 1981.\nPage: Winnie the Pooh and the Honey Tree. Sentence: Its songs were written by the Sherman Brothers (Richard M. Sherman and Robert B. Sherman) and the score was composed and conducted by Buddy Baker.",
